{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1534165-dark-eras-2-death-wolf-s-sheut","id":1534165,"title":"[Dark Eras 2] Death Wolf's Sheut","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-13T15:55:51-07:00","id":1534165,"title":"[Dark Eras 2] Death Wolf's Sheut","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> The Dark Eras 2 writeup of Death Wolf Sheut is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Opener of the Way</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death Wolf\u2019s Sheut is an immensely powerful<br /> ghost, all white fur, ice-blue eyes, and snapping<br /> jaws. Like Death Wolf in this era, the ghost is a<br /> Rank 7 entity, though it has not yet come into<br /> its full power, only recently having attained its<br /> current Rank. It cannot yet enter the world of the<br /> living \u2014 no mere Avernian Gate can withstand<br /> its metaphysical weight \u2014 but when it does, it is<br /> too powerful for Uratha to face directly unless<br /> they can find its Bane or weaken it with rites and<br /> potent hekau.</div> </div> </div> </div>My questions are a bit disorganized but essentially amount to:<b> Why and how does a Spirit have a Ghost?</b><br /> <br /> Do spirits (at least those above Rank 5), have the Fivefold soul of Mummy?<br /> <br /> Can Death Wolf (or any other Firstborn, Rank 6+ spirit) create &quot;copies&quot; of themselves with other template? i.e. If you are a Rank 7 spirit, can you get also get a Rank 7 Ghost of yourself?<br /> <br /> What happened with this Rnak 7 ghost? Is it part of the Bone Shadows pact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T18:02:22-07:00","id":1534174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1534165-dark-eras-2-death-wolf-s-sheut#post1534165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,My questions are a bit disorganized but essentially amount to:<b> Why and how does a Spirit have a Ghost?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Because Death Wolf is a particularly powerful spirit whose origins as the child of a Pangaean give her the metaphysical anatomy that makes it possible for spiritual trauma such as that brought on by untimely death to create a self-willed double that inhabits the deathly frequencies of reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do spirits (at least those above Rank 5), have the Fivefold soul of Mummy? </div> </div> </div>Spirits are identified as the Ka of the things they are born from in Mummy's view of the Shadow. Notably, Mekhet: Shadows in the Dark contains a primer on ancient Egyptian soul anatomy (pages 12 and 13); as described in the Era itself, a ghost is usually seen as the Ka sundered from the body and denied nourishment; the Ka of a Hollow Mekhet is the hungry ghost that haunts them (in addition to bearing their shadow, echo, and reflection), and that primer identifies the Ka as the Soul of Sustenance (and, less relevantly, the Ba as the Soul of Mobility).<br /> <br /> This further jives with faith, trust, loyalty, confidence, and similar terms resonating with those mummies who declared their Essence as the defining Pillar of their soul, because the Essence that sustains ghosts is described in Geist as coming from &quot;the instinctive expectation for something to be present&quot; while knowing it won't be. The Ka marks the difference between a thing that is living and a thing that is dead.<br /> <br /> Death Wolf, at least, has a fivefold soul as far as it serves to explain that part of the scenario in Hunger in the Black Land \u2014 when she was Seeking Wolf and entered the Underworld and died, she seized her Essence and most of her Heart with the remainder serving to give malignant will to her Shadow, which dwells in the Underworld as an equally powerful ghost while she returned to life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can Death Wolf (or any other Firstborn, Rank 6+ spirit) create &quot;copies&quot; of themselves with other template? i.e. If you are a Rank 7 spirit, can you get also get a Rank 7 Ghost of yourself? </div> </div> </div>Death Wolf's ghost was explicitly created from the spiritual violence of her dying and coming back to life. As a lesser Ilusah, within the bounds of her thematic Influences she has the capacity to mess with templates and the interactions of relevant phenomena with subjects, as well as creating self-perpetuating phenomena, but &quot;a godlike being accidentally created an equally powerful evil ghost of herself&quot; is a freak accident that her part in the events of the Era itself is mostly concerned with attempting to reverse that process. It's conceivable that e.g. Silver Wolf might incarnate a portion of his nature into a Deviant, but divine politics and the division of the worlds mean most instances of a god duplicating itself with key differences are going to be either strange events like this or the product of long and careful negotiations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What happened with this Rnak 7 ghost? Is it part of the Bone Shadows pact? </div> </div> </div>Per the Era's &quot;What Is To Come&quot; section:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The years are not kind to Shedet or Hawara. While Sobekneferu still lives, the conflict between the cults of Sobek and Wepwawet comes to a head \u2014 and the children of Crocodile falter. For all their blasphemous might, the spirit magic of the Forsaken and the treachery of the Pure are their undoing. Death Wolf descends upon Hawara, hungry for reunion with her wayward Sheut. In desperation, the crocodile priests attempt one grotesque last gasp of fusion between their rotting god and the divine symbolism of the pharaonic mantle. Sobekneferu does not survive, and with her dies their hope. The werewolves bury Crocodile once more, and the Sobeki scatter.<br /> <br /> The werewolves bury Crocodile once more, and the Sobeki scatter. In the hour of her triumph, Death Wolf is also denied her prize; the god\u2019s mad Sheut slips the grasp of her jaws, glutted on Crocodile\u2019s Essence and stronger than the Firstborn expects it to be. She howls her frustration, and the Shadow shakes. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-13T22:23:39-07:00","id":1534181,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, so what I am getting is that there is a Rank 7 Ghost somewhere that has the memories of Death Wolf and it has feed on a Pangaean power?<br /> <br /> <br /> What is the expected result if Death Wolf consumes or merges their Sheut Ghost? A rank increase? Becoming the strongest of the Firstborn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-14T06:47:03-07:00","id":1534189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1534165-dark-eras-2-death-wolf-s-sheut?p=1534181#post1534181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answer <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>, so what I am getting is that there is a Rank 7 Ghost somewhere that has the memories of Death Wolf and it has feed on a Pangaean power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I missed a follow-up note from a chronologically later Dark Era, yeah, that's the size of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is the expected result if Death Wolf consumes or merges their Sheut Ghost? A rank increase? Becoming the strongest of the Firstborn? </div> </div> </div>Per her described motivations, if Death Wolf reintegrates her Sheut she reaps the benefit of its having learned a bunch of deathly lore that she hasn't been able to get at; presumably at the very least this opens up mystical avenues that she didn't have before, which might results in the precedents for new Rites being established, new Merits for Bone Shadows like those introduced for the Predator Kings and Ivory Claws in Shunned by the Moon, or some other strangeness relating to ghosts and/or the Underworld having her metaphorical pawprints on it.<br /> <br /> It would have to go to the judges whether one of the Firstborn eating their spiritual double is sufficiently close to a fundamental alteration of the universe to close the gulf in power between a lesser Ilusah and the likes of Luna, Helios, or even Mother Ocean, but personally I wouldn't mark that out as grounds for a bump to Rank 8 on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T16:08:40-08:00","id":1548240,"title":"","content":"Satchel covered the question on a technical level perfectly. To add my own meandering home brew to an otherwise perfectly logical and better answer: I've been reading the high end / tier 4 material for Chronicles (mostly 1st Ed. but also a bit of VtR and Chronicles Core) and noticed shared motifs between game lines and their inspirations, so let me offer my interpretation.<br /> <br /> At its core, Chronicles presents a Sundered World. The Essential plane ripped from it's Quintessential components, basically organs of a perfected being / rank 10, yet those pieces still seek to synchronize with their Essence. These Quintessential Pieces would be spirits comparable in power to Wyld, Wyrm, and Weaver of WoD but are never named, stuff like Arcadia, the Underworld, the Shadow, etc. So, when I have a Rank 6+, what I mean is I have a piece of Shadow so quintessentially bound to the operations of the dynamic world that it has anchors beyond the Shadow, that the other planes are so interconnected to this being that destroying it isn't possible unless all of those interconnected sympathies are also destroyed. What's more, given enough time, those connections alone will reconstitute entities at that power level; granted they will return in a form based on the mutual relation between those connections rather than the being in question.<br /> <br /> Example: Old Slick: he is the shock felt just after the car crash. She is wet blood felt while staring in disbelief at a severed hand. The Horseman of Nature's patient warden who waits with the dying, allowing their mind to rest after being too shocked or narrow in scope to realize the presence in the room. Old Slick is a minor god of the Underworld but is still tethered more to the Astral as it spends most of its time permeating the awareness of mortals rather than in the Underworld. As such, if its avatar is summoned, it behaves in a manner based on how mortals closely related to the viewer perceive this embodiment of Death in their own lives rather than the anything the Underworld or mythologies have to say. While it is possible to travel into the Astral and destroy Slick's presence in the World Soul, unless you cease all mortals from processing &quot;shock&quot; in death once Slick is reduced to no health, but Slick will naturally reform as souls pour into the Upper Mysteries leaving an impression that will manifest into a more Cthonic form of Slick during the scene. Over the course of a session or two it will reform into the exact same entity to be found in the exact same astral realm.<br /> <br /> So, Death Wolf. I mean, yeah, Pangaean / first born whatever. But I would suggest the reason that definition matters is because it means Death Wolf didn't exist purely of the Shadow (like an antediluvian may bond with the living world and archmages bond with the supernal), she had a matrix of patterns that constituted her essential being. Basically a soul, but like, it takes up real estate in the invisible realms/ parent spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6516,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6516-mefathiel8","user":"mefathiel8","date":". 02-05-2025, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6516-mefathiel8","name":"mefathiel8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T10:01:48-08:00","id":1548259,"title":"","content":"So I'm surprised no one mentions the last time Death Wolf's ghost/sheut* showed up, being The Great War, where in the warfront drew Death Wolf and Sheut Wolf into grand conflict. The era openly acknowledges that Seeking Wolf having a ghost is impossible, and also acknowledges that that fact is useless in the face of Sheut Wolf still existing despite the impossibility. Sheut Wolf is also strongly implied to have survived the era, and likely into the modern day. SO, yeah, check it out.<br /> <br /> *in as much as I need to refer to it in this post, I will reference it as Sheut Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T06:01:22-08:00","id":1548289,"title":"","content":"I'm also curious, Death Wolf in Kemet needs a host to get into the flesh side to track down her trapped ghost. The best host option is implied to be Ptahneferu, sister of the Pharoah and a promethean. Clearly Death Wolf failed in Egypt but if she did bond with Ptahneferu, what happened to the royal? Hell, what would the effect of bonding with a firstborn be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T11:28:58-08:00","id":1548298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1534165-dark-eras-2-death-wolf-s-sheut?p=1548289#post1548289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also curious, Death Wolf in Kemet needs a host to get into the flesh side to track down her trapped ghost. The best host option is implied to be Ptahneferu, sister of the Pharoah and a promethean. Clearly Death Wolf failed in Egypt but if she did bond with Ptahneferu, what happened to the royal? Hell, what would the effect of bonding with a firstborn be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally, You'd get a god incarnated, the process of claiming the corpse warping it and destroying it beyond recognition, but Death Wolf would be able to bring their Influences to bear much more directly, trading the spiritual devastation of Death Wolf's presence in the Shadow for a more directed but still devastating mini-apocalypse. It wouldn't be bad on the scale of Sheut Wolf claiming Crocodile's corpse, but the fact that this was Death Wolf's answer to that possibly happening tells you just how cataclysmic having Death Wolf incarnate could be.<br /> <br /> THat said, since Ptahneferu was actually a Promethean at the time, it likely would have gotten worse. The story seed mentions surmising that the Divine Fire-powered corpse might actually be all the more sustainable for the Firstborn, but even as that level of power begins to break down the differences between worlds and types, the Divine Fire is one of those things that likely remains a concern for entities like that, and of all the Firstborn I would guess might have a safer time being adjacent to and possibly utilizing the Azoth of a corpse, Death Wolf lands low on the list. It would mean that Death Wolf Incarnated would be all the more powerful, but would be subject to warp and change, and the alchemically poisoned Influences and spiritual empowered Wastelands would be be something of a weirdmageddon.<br /> <br /> It'd be bad either way, and likely the Promethean called Ptahneferu wouldn't emerge from the incident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}